  "description": "Per-block Fréchet test of the μ₃ sign door on the adjacent H₉ |χ|-joint-trace. Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.lean proves Δ² is linear over Wedderburn blocks and that a block is submodular iff its joint damping falls below the Fréchet–Hoeffding lower bound r_a+r_b−1; the per-block Δ²|χ|_λ sign is therefore exactly the per-block Fréchet test on the geometry. Gated on (i) linearity Σ_λΔ²_λ = Δ²g, (ii) the factorisation Δ²_λ = y_λ·Δ²|χ|_λ, and (iii) the #4404 baseline c₃ = −1.769 (T) / −1.405 (³He). No fit, nothing wired.",
